    "Read all four complete candidate sources (148+123+118+110=499 lines), every exact diff, both actual main consumer files, the full main CanonicalStripGeometry and CanonicalBoundaryImage, and the actual-domain CanonicalGeometry chart/boundary contracts.",
    "Each before file equals the exact Git source at c6c8f4881c127c415919addae844aee8422e4548. Every recorded source/diff SHA256, Git blob and line count matches the bytes; each stored diff is exactly regenerated from its before/after files.",
    "CanonicalBoundaryImage changes only the body of canonicalChart_endpoint_radial_eq_boundary. That complete declaration and proof are byte-identical to main ebfd528f. It uses the actual physical frontier, closed forward smoothness, the open inverse and closure uniqueness; no rectangular assumption is added for a negative current piece.",
    "The generic boundary helper, rectangular endpoint helper and both branch-specific positive-piece specializations are retained unchanged. In particular canonicalPhysicalPieceClosed_of_positive and canonicalChart_positive_endpoint_radial_eq_boundary are byte-identical to the before file, so their actual-domain consumers remain available.",
    "Exactly three public headers are generalized: chart_angle_eq_zero_of_reflection, chart_angle_mem_Ioo_iff and chart_angle_mem_openInterval_iff replace a radial Ioo(a,b) by an arbitrary A:Set Real. The reflection local membership type is changed consistently; all other proof steps stay unchanged. No openness or connectedness of A is used: the proof follows the full angular fiber over a fixed radius in A.",
    "The reflection/injectivity argument identifies the zero angular fiber for arbitrary A. The retained periodic-lift theorem then gives both directions of angular interval membership from the same actual fibers. The wrapper uses the positive period to obtain its nonzero premise. All eight main public CanonicalStripGeometry headers are present exactly once across the retained split modules and match the main headers byte-for-byte.",
    "All 17 existing public declaration names are retained, with no additions or removals; the other 14 full public headers and all imports/options remain byte-identical. The main monolithic declarations are not copied into the split module, so the known duplicate public names are avoided.",
    "All direct uses of the three generalized APIs in both the baseline tree and fixed main were inspected. Their radial set is inferred from InjOn/ContinuousOn/membership arguments; no caller supplies the removed named a/b binders. Existing Ioo callers specialize A=Ioo, while N05 closed-boundary callers require and correctly infer A=Icc.",
    "N06CurrentChartChange uses the open canonical cylinder and actual inverse on moving physical domains. Its two generalized angular calls retain all arguments, and inverseChart_periodic_of_chart_periodic_on and the original strip-to-strip interface remain unchanged.",
    "N05CanonicalBoundarySymmetry uses the genuine closed inverse and its closed period/reflection identities. The generalized reflection and angular-interval lemmas now apply directly to canonicalClosed=Icc(left,right) times univ, including both radial endpoints. No closed inverse value is replaced by a reference-only value."
